<title>KUWAIT: TABLE-Kuwait Finance House 1H up 15.8pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Kuwait Finance House 1H up 15.8pct.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six month to June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>					     (Million dinars)</p>
<p>					1997			1996</p>
<p> Net profit			 14.10		     12.17</p>
<p> Net murabaha, leasing income 43.10		     36.73</p>
<p> Gross operating income	 55.24		     51.10</p>
<p> Murabaha receivables	1,004.16		    839.78</p>
<p> Government debt bonds	 197.19		    255.94</p>
<p> Reserves			   48.71		     41.18</p>
<p> Total assets		  1,496.87		  1,372.74</p>
<p> Earnings per share (fils)     27.88		     25.51</p>
<p> Market price per share (fils)   960			 630</p>
<p>Full name: Kuwait Finance House (K.S.C.)</p>
<p>Note - Kuwait finance house operates according to Islamic banking rules which ban interest. It shares profits with depositors. Government institutions own 49 percent of the company which was founded in 1997.</p>
<p>(1,000 fils to the dinar)</p>
